88,"seed":1050160353603379086,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\), we will calculate the product step by step and then specifically focus on the last three digits (hundreds, tens, and units digits).\n\n1. First, calculate the product of the numbers:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 6 = 30\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 7 = 210\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   210 \\times 8 = 1680\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1680 \\times 9 = 15120\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   15120 \\times 10 = 151200\n   \\]\n\n2. The product is \\(151200\\). To find the hundreds digit, we look at the last three digits of the product, which are \\(200\\).\n\n3. The hundreds digit of \\(200\\) is \\(2\\).\n\nThus, the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\), we will calculate the product step by step and then specifically focus on the last three digits (hundreds, tens, and units digits).\n\n1. First, calculate the product of the numbers:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 6 = 30\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 7 = 210\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   210 \\times 8 = 1680\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1680 \\times 9 = 15120\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   15120 \\times 10 = 151200\n   \\]\n\n2. The product is \\(151200\\). To find the hundreds digit, we look at the last three digits of the product, which are \\(200\\).\n\n3. The hundreds digit of \\(200\\) is \\(2\\).\n\nThus, the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).","id":"number_theory:510"}
